      "name": null,
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{6},$ then $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+10\\pi )+2=$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{6},$ then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+10\\pi )=-\\frac{5}{6}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+10\\pi )+2 & =-(-\\frac{5}{6})+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
